{"text": "4.\n\nOPEGA Review Request Form\n\nOffice of Program Evaluation and Government Accountability\n\nPlease complete this form with information that is as specific as possible. Use additional\npages as necessary. If you wish to submit your request in a letter please include as many\nof the details asked for on this form as possible. You may be contacted by OPEGA and\nasked for additional information. If you have questions about the form or the request\nprocess, please contact OPEGA at 207-287-1901.\n\n/ What the name the department, \u2018program or function that you want OPEGA to review/audit? i\n|, Rep. Jeffrey Timberlake, would like to formally request that OPEGA review/audit the Fund for Healthy Maine. | know a\n\nmajority of the money used to fund this program comes from the tobacco settlement, but | would like to know how much\ntaxpayer money is included as well.\n\nWhat concerns have led you to request an OPEGA review?\nThe Fund for Healthy Maine receives a significant amount of taxpayer dollars annually. As a member of the appropriations\ncommittee, | have sought answers to my questions, but have been unsuccessful. | have not been provided with a precise\nbreakdown of how the money is spent. Maine taxpayers deserve to know how their money is being used to ensure that it is\nbeing prioritized properly.\n\n\"What specific questions would you like an OPEGA review to answer? _\n1. How much money is given to the Fund for Healthy Maine annually?\nDoes appropriated money go into a separate bank account?\nHow much money is spent on administrative costs annually?\n\nOf the allocated money, how much is spent on projects/programs for Mainers?\n\n2\n3\n4\n5. What happens to the money that is unspent?\n6. How much money is allocated for Planned Parenthood?\n7. Does the Fund for Healthy Maine know where/how Planned Parenthood spends those funds?\n8\n\nDoes the Legislature supplement the Fund For Healthy Maine tobacco settlement money> If so, is\nthere a history of the allocations?\n\n9. Is there a list of recipients who have received Fund for Healthy Maine money? How much of those funds\nwere not spent and were returned to the Fund for Healthy Maine?\n\nWhat potential beneficial outcomes do you expect may come from OPEGA performing this review? :\n| believe that by conducting this review, money given to the Fund for Healthy Maine by the Legislature will be better\nprioritized. It is my hope that this review will help the Fund for Healthy Maine better serve the Maine taxpayer.",
"words": [
